                <head>PM–62. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>In an exchange of notes on October 31, 1960, between Joseph S. Farland, the
                    American Ambassador in Panama, and Galileo Solís, the Panamanian Minister of
                    Foreign Relations, the United States Government and the Republic of Panama
                    concluded an agreement that entered into force on October 31, 1960, whereby the
                    Canal Zone Government and the Republic of Panama established procedures for the
                    reciprocal recognition of motor vehicle operator’s licenses. For the texts of
                    the notes exchanged, see 12 UST 301.
                    Documentation concerning the negotiation of this agreement is in decimal file
                    611.1913.</p>
            </div>
